course: dictionary
lesson: 13744
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word intercept can mean stop something on its way, catch secret messages, or the point where a line crosses an axis on a graph. «The defender stepped in and intercepted the pass.» Here the ball was stopped on its way to a teammate.
explain: Check the clues around the word. In «The codebreakers intercepted enemy messages», the clue is messages, and intercepted means secretly caught messages that were meant for someone else. In «The line crosses the y-axis at 4, so the y-intercept is 4», the clue is the graph, and the y-intercept is the point where the line crosses the axis.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning. If it sounds silly, look again at the clue words and try a different meaning.
fact: Intercept is a verb: you intercept something, and it is often used with a pass in football or netball.
fact: Intercept can also be a noun, as in «the y-intercept» on a graph.
fact: «Intercept» means to stop something on the way and catch or block it before it gets where it was going.
fact: «Intercept» can also mean to secretly catch messages that were meant for someone else.
fact: In maths, «intercept» is the point where a line or graph crosses an axis.
exercise: «The goalkeeper moved fast and intercepted the pass before it reached the striker.» What does intercepted mean? | *Stopped and caught it on the way | Threw it out of the pitch | Kicked it into the net
exercise: «The line crosses the y-axis at 4. That point is the y-intercept.» What is a y-intercept? | A fast running shoe | *The point where a line crosses the y-axis | The top of a hill | A sharp pencil
exercise: «Spies tried to intercept the letter before it reached the general.» Find and copy the word that means to stop something on its way. | general | *intercept | letter | reached
test: «The codebreakers at Bletchley Park intercepted enemy messages.» What does intercepted mean here? | *Secretly caught messages meant for someone else | Sent messages to their friends | Wrote the messages out again | Lost the messages in the post
test: Ben says, «A defender can intercept a pass by stepping in front of it.» What does he mean? | Kicks the ball out of play | Passes the ball back to the goalkeeper | Throws the ball out of the field | *Blocks the ball on its way and takes it
exam: «The graph crosses the y-axis at 2, so its y-intercept is 2.» What does y-intercept mean? | *The point where the line crosses the y-axis | A type of graph paper | The highest point on the graph | The name of the axis
